WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.488
Every book in this workbook
moves a decision to someone.

2
00:00:03.488 --> 00:00:06.637
The help desk now verifies
before it resets.

3
00:00:06.637 --> 00:00:10.138
Administrators activate their
roles only when they need them.

4
00:00:10.138 --> 00:00:11.562
Owners approve access,

5
00:00:11.562 --> 00:00:15.462
and HR keeps the data that creates
accounts right at the source.

6
00:00:15.462 --> 00:00:20.700
Jobs split into deciding and doing, so
two people now need each procedure.

7
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.185
And decisions move to people outside IT,

8
00:00:23.185 --> 00:00:26.950
who need short training on the
one decision that's now theirs.

9
00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:32.315
So the first workforce decision belongs to
the chief human capital officer's office:

10
00:00:32.315 --> 00:00:35.381
draft the roster of everyone
whose work changes,

11
00:00:35.381 --> 00:00:38.600
from HR and identity records,
before the first gate.

12
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.700
Next, why timing matters.
